    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 2/2 passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and the value is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` carry a `LocalDate registrationDate` (serialized by Jackson as `YYYY-MM-DD`). It's part of `OwnerFields`, so it's both accepted on create and returned on read via the `Owner` `allOf`.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it in both directions automatically (same name/type).\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after mapping the DTO to an `Owner`, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it's `null`; a supplied date is preserved.\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests use the hsqldb profile; the others are updated for consistency.\n\nVerified: `coreDefaultsToToday` (defaults to today when omitted) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (keeps `2020-06-15`) both pass, and the full suite is green.",
